Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:18:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: chapter markers on the audiobook player; fix engine
 create_vtt() calling missing _build_vtt_file

- build_vtt_file(): emit 'chapter <block>' WebVTT marker cues (start time + title of each block's first sentence, matching the embedded m4b/mp3 chapter tags) and accept pre-measured durations
- header.js: parseVTT() collects chapter cues into window.audiobook_chapters (kept out of the sentence cue list); render_chapter_marks() draws clickable tick marks under the player seek bar with hover titles, redrawn on loadedmetadata
- TTSUtils._build_vtt_file(): implement the method all 24 engine classes' create_vtt() called but that never existed (AttributeError whenever invoked)
- check_audiobook_hallucinations.py: skip chapter marker cues like interludes
---
 lib/classes/tts_engines/common/utils.py | 10 ++++
 lib/header.js                           | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/check_audiobook_hallucinations.py |  4 +-
 3 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/classes/tts_engines/common/utils.py b/lib/classes/tts_engines/common/utils.py
index 0ad6fb4..5a43034 100644
--- a/lib/classes/tts_engines/common/utils.py
+++ b/lib/classes/tts_engines/common/utils.py
@@ -198,6 +198,16 @@ class TTSUtils:
     engine_zs = None
     tts_zs_key = None
     vc_alerted = False
+
+    def _build_vtt_file(self, all_sentences:list)->bool:
+        # create_vtt() in the engine classes builds the per-preview vtt from the sentences
+        # just synthesized into session['sentences_dir'] (the audiobook-wide vtt with chapter
+        # markers is written by core.py calling build_vtt_file() directly)
+        built, error = build_vtt_file(self.session, block_indices=None, offsets=None, durations=None)
+        if not built:
+            print(error)
+        return bool(built)
+
     # voice file -> the one _check_xtts_builtin_speakers() gave for it, per engine instance (set by _set_voice())
     converted_voices = None
 
